.TH EVENT_LOOP_MODIFY 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
event_loop_modify \- change an existing fd registration's direction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t event_loop_modify(event_loop loop, event_reg *reg,
                        ccol_select_dir new_dir);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Changes reg's direction in place, without a window where the underlying
fd is briefly unregistered.  fd-only: called on a registration built
from a queue/channel selectable, returns ccol_invalid_args, since a
queue selectable's direction is part of its identity (remove and re-add
instead of modifying).

On success:
  - reg->sel.dir is updated.  A callback dispatched after this call
    returns observes the new direction via the sel parameter it
    receives (the dispatch path copies reg->sel under its own internal
    lock at the moment each dispatch is collected, not a live pointer
    into reg->sel, so a callback already in flight when this function
    is called deterministically keeps seeing whichever direction was
    current when it was collected, rather than racing this update).
  - reg moves to the other slot on its underlying fd's shared epoll
    entry.
  - The fd's combined epoll interest mask is recomputed via a single
    EPOLL_CTL_MOD call.

This is only valid when the target direction's slot is not already
occupied by a different registration on the same fd; use this to
implement, for example, a non-blocking connect that starts with
write-interest and switches to read-interest once the connect
completes, without needing two separate event_loop_add() calls.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
loop     event_loop the registration belongs to.
reg      Registration to modify.
new_dir  ccol_select_read or ccol_select_write.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        Direction changed.
ccol_invalid_args   loop is EVENT_LOOP_INVALID or a stale/already-
                    destroyed handle; reg is NULL; reg is a queue/
                    channel registration; new_dir is neither
                    ccol_select_read nor ccol_select_write; or reg was
                    concurrently removed (by another thread, or by
                    reg's own callback self-removing) between the
                    caller obtaining it and this call.
ccol_not_permitted  The target direction is already occupied by a
                    different registration on the same fd.
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
.nf
Safe to call concurrently with event_loop_remove() and from within a
callback running on one of the reactor threads.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
event_handlers_t handlers = { .on_writable = on_connected, .on_readable = on_data };
event_reg *reg = event_loop_add(loop, selectable_from_fd(sock, ccol_select_write),
                                handlers, ctx, NULL);
/* ... inside on_connected, once the non-blocking connect completes ... */
event_loop_modify(loop, reg, ccol_select_read);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR event_loop_add (3),
.BR event_loop_remove (3),
